  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating the number of favorable comparisons between maximum and minimum outcomes. The individual did not consider or mention the maximum or minimum outcomes at all. Instead, their justification is based entirely on the difference in probabilities (34% vs. 33%), which is unrelated to the reason’s rule. The reason’s rule would lead to preferring A due to its higher maximum, but the individual preferred B based on probability alone. The information considered (probabilities) and the justification (higher chance to win) do not align with the decision reason’s criteria (comparison of max/min outcomes). Therefore, the individual did not use this decision reason. However, there is no explicit contradiction or mention of the outcomes, so it is not certain that the reason was completely ruled out in the background—though the reported deliberation shows no trace of it. The assessment leans toward 'not used' but with slight uncertainty due to potential unreported cognitive processes.",
